    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8454" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεπι-τήδευτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>made without
			care</i> or <i>design, artless,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				22
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Onos.
				10.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				44
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1.156
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Pisc.</u>
				12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>unpractised, untried,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέν ἀμίμητον οὐδ᾽ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					23
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως, γλώττης οὐκ ἀ. εἶχεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					7.27
				</span></i>
			.</div>
